# Escape Room Game Logic Rules

## Game Flow & Progression

- Players start at room 1 and progress sequentially through rooms 1-12
- Each room must be completed before accessing the next
- Game state is managed in [src/store/gameStore.ts](mdc:src/store/gameStore.ts)
- Progress is persisted to localStorage for session recovery

## Hint System

- Total of 3 hints available across all rooms (shared pool)
- Hints are consumed immediately when used
- Hint count is tracked in global game state
- Each room has a specific hint defined in [src/lib/rooms.ts](mdc:src/lib/rooms.ts)

## Room Data Structure

- Room definitions in [src/lib/rooms.ts](mdc:src/lib/rooms.ts) follow the Room interface from [src/types/room.ts](mdc:src/types/room.ts)
- Each room has: id, title, question, answer, hint, type, difficulty
- Difficulty ranges from 3-10 as specified in [spec.md](mdc:spec.md)
- Answers are case-sensitive strings

## Puzzle Types & Implementation

- Pattern recognition (rooms 1, 8)
- Logic puzzles (rooms 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11)
- Time-based puzzles (room 3)
- Mathematical puzzles (rooms 7, 11)
- Visual puzzles (rooms 10, 12)
- Card-based puzzles (separate game in [src/app/games/card/](mdc:src/app/games/card/))

## Session Management

- Player sessions include: name, start/end time, browser info, IP
- Redis integration for leaderboard and analytics (via NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL)
- Automatic logging on room entry/exit for analytics
